Lab 14: Manage Automation Controller Projects
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Create and configure new projects in Ansible Automation Controller
Link projects to Git repositories for source control integration
Create and configure job templates for running Ansible playbooks
Understand the relationship between projects, inventories, and job templates
Execute automated tasks using the Automation Controller web interface
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Ansible concepts (playbooks, roles, inventories)
Familiarity with Git version control system
Knowledge of YAML syntax
Understanding of Linux command line operations
Access to a web browser for the Automation Controller interface
Lab Environment
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with Ansible Automation Controller already installed. Simply click Start Lab to begin - no need to build your own virtual machine or install software.

Your lab environment includes:

